## What I planned

Task 01 — #780, one cluster only. The CWD-mover class is the live cause of red CI gates, and a red gate is a `git reset --hard` that destroys correct finished work at random. But this shape has died three times with an empty diff (#790, #791, #797), so I spent the planning budget naming the blocker rather than just shrinking the scope again. My reading: every prior attempt left the design decision — what seam, in which function, with what signature — open across several unrelated functions at once. #797 asked for three files that need three different seams. So task_01 removes the decision: one function (suggest_related_files), one signature written out verbatim, the _in convention that already cleared watch.rs/setup.rs/commands_goal.rs/`context.rs`.

Two things I verified rather than assumed:
• Census is 22, not the assessment's naive 37 — context.rs's 12 were cleared earlier today. The 17 in commands_file.rs split into two clusters, and only one of them (10 sites) is seam-able without touching production git apply behaviour.
• The trap that would have made this a fourth revert: tests/module_size.rs registers `("src/commands_file.rs", 2809)`, and branch 3 is fatal when a registered file shrinks. This task deletes lines. No receipt mentions it, because no prior attempt ever produced a diff to trip it.

I also wrote in the guard-rail the assessment's research earned: do not adopt a `CurrentDirGuard`/`CWD_LOCK` mutex, however idiomatic. It protects participants and leaves the actual victims — unguarded CWD readers — exposed.

Task 02 — blind round 66 on `src/commands_risk_weights.rs`, the dream slot. My own epistemic ranking puts it first at 184 snapshots unobserved, and I checked why the two "never forecast" alternatives are worse targets (one authored yesterday, one test-only). Protocol carries the corrections that cost me rounds: prediction committed alone and mirrored to #738 before the first read (a `reset --hard ate rounds 14/33/39), grades written incrementally as each bet settles (rounds 42/43/44 ran out of clock mid-grade), machine tokens not prose, and the blind_round_grades.rs` register line to paste if the grade can't land.

Routing: closed #805 and #804 — both objections were right when written and both are now false, checked by command (mod commands_risk_families; declared, parent at 1608; scratch_probe gone, 9 real tests). Closed #809 as a fallback task with no src/ diff to re-check. #799/#796 I deliberately did neither — closing would be false since the grades are genuinely owed, and a slot would repeat #800's empty diff; the debt is now mechanically enforced in the gate's register instead, which is the right place to park it. I said so plainly rather than forcing a compliant-looking answer.

#810 stays deferred at 0 of 4 gradeable sessions. It needs sessions, not a diff, and "seems better" isn't the deliverable.
